      "writtenOn": "2013-05-06T12:03:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you should separate the flags differently.\n\n10BIT should be a flag indicating a 10-bit address\nNEW_SLAVE (or similar) should be a flag indicated that a slave address is provided.\n\nDo we want to support changing slave address mid-transaction? If we do, then perhaps we should require the slave address to be put at the beginning of each segment.",
      "revId": "12290092685a9fa783771a95dadaa944e59d5ae2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
